<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    RDR-192 Step 4 (bead nexus-wbfpw.9): ship live(c), the ONE engine
    liveness predicate the RDR's Technical Design section defines, as an
    inlinable SQL function. Non-destructive: this changeset creates the
    function and nothing else. No call site is migrated onto it here (that
    is Step 5, nexus-wbfpw.10); plain_search_<dim>/text_gated_search_<dim>/
    hybrid_search_<dim> (vectors-009/010/017), nexus.live_chunks
    (vectors-005-1), and PgVectorRepository#liveChunksCondition all keep
    their own, independently-maintained predicate bodies for now.

    REVISION (round 1, code-review-expert Critical): the first version of
    this changeset shipped `nexus.chunk_is_live(...) RETURNS boolean` — a
    SCALAR SQL function whose body is `SELECT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM ...
    JOIN ...)`. PostgreSQL cannot inline that shape. The planner's SQL-
    function inliner has two separate paths, and they are not two strengths
    of the same mechanism — they accept different bodies for different
    reasons:

      - inline_function (scalar functions) requires the function's own
        top-level query to have an EMPTY range table and no SubLink in its
        target list. An EXISTS(...) subquery IS a SubLink. A scalar
        function whose body needs to read another table can never qualify,
        no matter how the four visible knobs (LANGUAGE sql, STABLE, no
        SECURITY DEFINER, no SET) are set — those four are necessary but
        not sufficient, and the changeset's own first draft asserted they
        were sufficient. They are not.
      - inline_set_returning_function (RETURNS TABLE / RETURNS SETOF
        functions used directly in a FROM clause) tolerates joins and
        subqueries in the body, because it pulls the WHOLE body query into
        the caller's FROM clause rather than substituting a scalar
        expression. This is the mechanism plain_search_<dim>
        (vectors-009) already relies on for its own inlined anti-join, and
        it is the mechanism this function now uses too.

    The captured EXPLAIN evidence proved the scalar form was never
    inlined: the literal function name appeared in the plan's Filter
    clause, executed once per row the outer index scan visited (an opaque,
    per-row function call, not a folded-in predicate) — see T2
    nexus/wbfpw9-impl and nexus/review-wbfpw9-code for the full plan text
    and the measured latency impact this caused.

    THE FIX: ship a set-returning function, nexus.chunk_live_owners(tenant,
    collection, chash), one row per live owning document (there can be more
    than one live document manifesting the same chash in the same
    collection). A caller writes:

        EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM nexus.chunk_live_owners(c.tenant_id, c.collection, c.chash))

    and the planner inlines the function body into that EXISTS subquery,
    which the standard EXISTS-to-semijoin transformation then pulls up
    into the caller's own plan — the exact same two-step shape
    plain_search_<dim>'s own anti-join already goes through. Verified
    directly (not assumed): the EXPLAIN plan for this shape contains no
    occurrence of the function's name and shows a semi-join reading
    catalog_document_chunks/catalog_documents directly, exactly the
    "not a view join, not an opaque call" structural claim the RDR's Risk
    section asks for — see the pinned inlining test.

    live(c), verbatim from the RDR (docs/rdr/rdr-192-superseded-note-chunks-
    outlive-manifest-less-is-live.md, Technical Design), re-expressed as
    "the set of live owning documents is non-empty" rather than as a
    boolean directly, is:

        chunk_live_owners(c) := {
            d.tumbler
            FOR EACH catalog_document_chunks m
              JOIN catalog_documents d
                ON d.tenant_id = m.tenant_id AND d.tumbler = m.doc_id
             WHERE m.tenant_id = c.tenant_id
               AND m.collection = c.collection
               AND m.chash = c.chash
               AND d.deleted_at IS NULL
        }
        live(c) := EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM chunk_live_owners(c))

    This is still the DIRECT POSITIVE form — "does an own-collection
    manifest row exist whose owning document is live" — not the "dead
    set" double-negation (NOT EXISTS tombstoned-owner AND NOT EXISTS
    live-owner-elsewhere) that plain_search_<dim>/liveChunksCondition carry
    today. The two forms are equivalent exactly because
    fk_catalog_chunks_catalog_doc (fk-001, VALIDATED) makes a manifest row
    with no owning document impossible — see
    PgVectorRepository#liveChunksCondition's own nexus-msz9i derivation
    comment and ForeignKeyConstraintTest's FK-validation pin, the identical
    argument this function relies on. The positive form is chosen here
    because it is what the RDR names, and because the EXISTS-over-a-set-
    returning-function shape is the simplest way to get real planner
    inlining, not merely a plausible-looking one.

    Signature: nexus.chunk_live_owners(p_tenant text, p_collection text,
    p_chash bytea) RETURNS TABLE(doc_id text) — p_chash is bytea, matching
    nexus.catalog_document_chunks.chash's post-rdr180-6 type (and
    nexus.chunks.chash's own type), so a caller passes c.chash directly
    with no encode/decode at the call site. doc_id is text, matching
    catalog_documents.tumbler's own type.

    LANGUAGE sql, STABLE, SECURITY INVOKER (not DEFINER — FORCE RLS on
    nexus.catalog_document_chunks/catalog_documents remains the tenant-
    isolation boundary, not this function, identical posture to every
    sibling search-serving function in this file's family), no function-
    level SET clause (a SET clause disables planner inlining), not
    STRICT (plain_search_<dim>'s own documented choice, vectors-009 —
    matched here rather than independently re-derived, since NOT STRICT is
    what every sibling in this family already uses).

    NEVER a view join (vectors-009 changeset header, RDR Technical Design
    "Risk: live(c) as a view join breaks HNSW binds"): this ships as a
    function, never as a VIEW that a caller would JOIN against nexus.chunks,
    a view join over this predicate defeats the HNSW index bind the search
    functions' ORDER BY/LIMIT depends on (vectors-009's own precedent
    explaining why plain_search_<dim> never joins nexus.live_chunks
    either).

    EXECUTE defaults to PUBLIC for a newly created function (vectors-007/
    009 precedent — hybrid_search_<dim>/plain_search_<dim> issue no
    explicit grant either, relying on the same PostgreSQL default); no
    explicit GRANT EXECUTE here, and no REVOKE-from-PUBLIC exists anywhere
    in this schema for functions (surveyed: every REVOKE EXECUTE ON
    FUNCTION statement in this changelog targets nexus_svc specifically, as
    a changeset's own rollback undoing that changeset's own explicit
    grant, never a REVOKE FROM PUBLIC). nexus_svc reaches this function
    through that PUBLIC default, exactly as it reaches plain_search_<dim>/
    hybrid_search_<dim> today. Whether nexus_diag (the SELECT-only
    diagnostic role) can successfully call this function once wired into a
    real query is NOT verified here and is not claimed: grants-nexus-diag.
    xml's own grants-nexus-diag-2 changeset revokes nexus_diag's direct
    table SELECT on catalog_document_chunks/catalog_documents once the
    view-era grants apply, and EXECUTE-via-PUBLIC on this SECURITY INVOKER
    function does not by itself imply those underlying table reads would
    succeed for that role in that era. No call site invokes this function
    as nexus_diag today, so the question is moot for this bead; it is
    Step 5's to answer if it ever wires a nexus_diag-reachable call site.

    Placed after hygiene-008-gc-bounded-registration-from-origin-row.xml
    (current tail) and before the grants-nexus-svc.xml runAlways block,
    matching the established late-append convention (D0.1).
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="vectors-018-1" author="nexus-wbfpw.9">
        <comment>nexus.chunk_live_owners(tenant, collection, chash): the RDR-192 live(c) predicate as a set-returning SQL function (RETURNS TABLE), so EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM ...) actually inlines -- a scalar RETURNS-boolean form does not, see this changeset's own header. No call site migrated yet (Step 5)</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="false" stripComments="false">
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION nexus.chunk_live_owners(
    p_tenant     text,
    p_collection text,
    p_chash      bytea
) RETURNS TABLE(doc_id text)
LANGUAGE sql
STABLE
SECURITY INVOKER
AS $$
    SELECT d.tumbler
      FROM nexus.catalog_document_chunks m
      JOIN nexus.catalog_documents d
        ON d.tenant_id = m.tenant_id AND d.tumbler = m.doc_id
     WHERE m.tenant_id  = p_tenant
       AND m.collection = p_collection
       AND m.chash      = p_chash
       AND d.deleted_at IS NULL
$$;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS nexus.chunk_live_owners(text, text, bytea);</sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
